+## Mode file
+
+In mode `file` a container gets the memory of a device (a shared or exclusive pool device, or a
+slice of a local memdev) as a read-only regular file of the size of the device,
+`$CXL_<KEY>_PATH` (`/run/cxl-files/<KEY>/data`). Programs open, read and `mmap` it like any
+file, so a program that loads a model or a data set from a file works on it unmodified. The node
+reads the file through its page cache: the first access to a page copies it from the device into
+the DRAM of the node, and later accesses, also by other containers on the node, use that copy.
+In mode `dax` a container maps the device itself: every access goes to the device, and nothing is
+cached.
+
+| | `dax` | `file` |
+|:-|:------|:-------|
+| the container gets | `/dev/daxX.Y`, a device node | `/run/cxl-files/<KEY>/data`, a file in a read-only bind mount |
+| access | `mmap` only (`MAP_SHARED`, aligned to the device alignment) | `read`, `mmap` (shared or private), any offset |
+| writes | unless `readOnly: true` | never: `readOnly: true` is required |
+| memory of the node | none | page cache, up to the size of the device on each node that reads it |
+| a change of the device's bytes | seen at once | not seen in pages that the node has cached |
+
+The node plugin prepares the device as for `dax` (a devdax device, never onlined; a local slice is
+zeroed), maps it read-only, and serves it as the file `data` of a read-only FUSE file system that
+it mounts in the host mount namespace at
+`/var/lib/kubelet/plugins/cxl.generic/files/<daxX.Y>/` (type `fuse.cxl-file`). There is one such
+export per dax device on the node, whatever the number of claims that use it; the last of them
+that is unprepared unmounts it. The CDI device of the claim bind-mounts that directory at
+`/run/cxl-files/<KEY>` (`rbind`, `ro`, `nosuid`, `nodev`, `noexec`). The container needs no
+device node, no device cgroup rule and no privileges. On SELinux hosts the files have the label
+`container_file_t`.
+
+The plugin logs the life of every export; `reads` and `bytes` count the read requests that the
+export served and the bytes it read from the device, that is what the node copied into its page
+cache:
+
+```
+file export: dax0.0: started (/dev/dax0.0, 536870912 bytes) at /var/lib/kubelet/plugins/cxl.generic/files/dax0.0/data for claim <uid> of cxl-pool.generic in 1.395ms
+file export: dax0.0: claim <uid2> of cxl-pool.generic holds it (claims: 2; 4096 reads, 536870912 bytes so far)
+file export: dax0.0: claim <uid> of cxl-pool.generic released it (claims: 1; 4096 reads, 536870912 bytes so far)
+file export: dax0.0: stopped at /var/lib/kubelet/plugins/cxl.generic/files/dax0.0/data (claim <uid2> of cxl-pool.generic was the last holder; 4096 reads, 536870912 bytes) in 2.797ms
+```
+
+Pages of the file are charged to the memory cgroup of the container that reads them first (and
+count against its memory limit, as reclaimable page cache); other containers use them without a
+charge. A container whose limit is lower than what it reads drops pages and reads them from the
+device again.
+
+Limitations:
+
+- Read-only. Cached pages are never refreshed: the content must not change while containers of
+  the node use the file. Write the device first (a claim in mode `dax` with all `hosts` of a
+  shared device), then read it in mode `file`.
+- A program that maps the file with `MAP_POPULATE` or reads it whole (llama.cpp does) copies the
+  whole device into the page cache when it starts, not page by page. Size the device close to the
+  data.
+- The plugin serves the file. While it is stopped or restarting, reads of pages that the node has
+  not cached fail (`EIO`; `SIGBUS` in a mapping); containers that started before keep failing so,
+  also after the restart, since their mount is of the stopped plugin. The restarted plugin exports
+  the device again for containers that start later: restart the containers that use the file
+  after a plugin restart.
+- An Unprepare whose export is in use on the node outside the claim's containers (the file is open
+  or mapped there, for example through the fd of a lease) fails, and kubelet retries.
+- The plugin must run as a host process in the host mount namespace ([Deploy](#deploy)).
+
